###
### Subify OS API — HTTP smoke tests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client)
###
### Preferred interactive UI (Development):
###   Scalar:     {{host}}/scalar/v1
###   OpenAPI:    {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
###   Root:       {{host}}/  → redirects to Scalar
###
### Run API:
###   cd api/Subify.Api && dotnet run --launch-profile http
###

@host = http://localhost:5240
@contentType = application/json

# After a successful login, paste tokens here for future authenticated requests:
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Docs — open Scalar UI in browser
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name scalarUi
GET {{host}}/scalar/v1
Accept: text/html

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Docs — OpenAPI document (JSON)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name openApiDocument
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Health — liveness (container probe)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name healthLive
GET {{host}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Health — readiness (Postgres reachable)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name healthReady
GET {{host}}/health/ready
Accept: application/json

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Setup — Status (3.3.6 / 3S.1)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name setupStatus
GET {{host}}/api/setup/status
Accept: application/json

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Setup — Create first SuperAdmin (3.3.1 / 3.3.6)
### Only while setup incomplete and no SuperAdmin yet
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name setupAdmin
POST {{host}}/api/setup/admin
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Super Admin",
  "email": "admin@test.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Register (3.2.1 / 3.3.2) — after setup + AllowPublicRegistration
### 403 AUTH_017 if setup incomplete (use /api/setup/admin first)
### 201 → User role only (never SuperAdmin)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Onur Karakuş",
  "email": "onur@test.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Register (duplicate email — expect 409)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name registerDuplicate
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Duplicate User",
  "email": "onur@test.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Login (3.2.2 / 3.2.10)
### 200 → { accessToken, refreshToken, expiration, user: { id, email, fullName, locale, roles, isSetupComplete } }
### 401 AUTH_001 · 423 AUTH_005
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "onur@test.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Login (invalid credentials — expect 401 / problem details)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name loginInvalid
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "onur@test.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword1!"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Login validation failure (empty body fields — expect 400 VAL)
### Pipeline: ValidationBehavior + LoginValidator → ProblemDetails.errors
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name loginValidationFail
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "",
  "password": ""
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Refresh token (3.2.3) — rotate after login
### Body: { refreshToken }
### 200 OK → { accessToken, refreshToken, expiration }
### 401 AUTH_004 invalid / AUTH_016 reuse (theft)
### Alias: POST /api/auth/refresh (same handler)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name refreshToken
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Refresh token alias
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name refreshTokenAlias
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken.response.body.$.refreshToken}}"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Logout (3.2.4)
### Body: { refreshToken } and/or { allSessions: true }
### 204 No Content
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name logout
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Change password (3.2.14) — requires Bearer
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name changePassword
POST {{host}}/api/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Password123!",
  "newPassword": "Password456!"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Admin — Reset user password (3.2.15) — SuperAdmin only
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name adminResetPassword
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/reset-password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "newPassword": "TempPass123!"
}
